Description: CVE-2024-11235 (GHSA-rwp7-7vc6-8477): the live range of the temporary that ZEND_SEPARATE defines again was ended there, which broke the handling of COPY_TMP: ??= on a property of the result of a call ($a->f()->p ??= ..., f()->p ??= ...), with __set or a typed property that throws, freed the value twice (a use-after-free). Fixed upstream in 8.3.19 and 8.4.5 only; the same code (zend_calc_live_ranges()) is in this branch
Origin: php-src commit ef2c459941b5ffae501e5311f5ac2041aadbe461 (Ilija Tovilo, 13.11.2024, PHP 8.3.19), as SUSE carries it for 7.4.33 and 8.0.30 (php7-CVE-2024-11235.patch, SLE 15) and Ubuntu for 7.4 (focal) and 8.1 (jammy) (CVE-2024-11235.patch); its three tests as Ubuntu's focal has them for 7.4: the method getFoo() for foo() (in 7.4 a method of the name of its class is a constructor of PHP 4, with a deprecation) and the message of 7.4 for a typed property

diff --git a/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_001.phpt b/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_001.phpt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..83d80323
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_001.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+--TEST--
+GHSA-rwp7-7vc6-8477: Use-after-free for ??= due to incorrect live-range calculation
+--FILE--
+<?php
+
+class Foo {
+    public function getFoo() {
+        return $this;
+    }
+
+    public function __set($name, $value) {
+        throw new Exception('Hello');
+    }
+}
+
+$foo = new Foo();
+
+try {
+    $foo->getFoo()->baz ??= 1;
+} catch (Exception $e) {
+    echo $e->getMessage();
+}
+
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+Hello
diff --git a/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_002.phpt b/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_002.phpt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5e11434c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Zend/tests/ghsa-rwp7-7vc6-8477_002.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+--TEST--
+GHSA-rwp7-7vc6-8477: Use-after-free for ??= due to incorrect live-range calculation
+--FILE--
+<?php
+
+class Foo {
+    public int $prop;
+
+    public function getFoo() {
+        return $this;
+    }
+}
+
+$foo = new Foo();
+
+try {
+    $foo->getFoo()->prop ??= 'foo';
+} catch (Error $e) {
+    echo $e->getMessage();
+}
+
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+Typed property Foo::$prop must be int, string used
